# Environment Variables Configuration

## Local Development
# No configuration needed connects to localhost automatically

## Production Deployment

### Option 1: Same domain (Recommended)
# If your React app is served from the same server as the game server, 
# no environment variables are needed. The app automatically connects to 
# the same host.

###Option 2: Separate domains
# If you host the React app on a different domain (e.g., Vercel/Metlify), "Vercel": Unknown
# you need to set the server URL:

# For React App (.env file in packages/web/):
REACT APP SERVER_URL=https://your-game-server.onrender.com

# For Game Server:
PORT=4500
NODE_ENV=production

# Hosting Platform Specific

### Render.com
# Set in render.yaml (already configured):
# - NODE ENV: production
# - PORT: 4500

### Railway.app
# Set in Railway dashboard:
# - NODE ENV: production
# - PORT: 4500

### Fly.io
# Set in fly.toml (already configured):
# - NODE ENV: production
# - PORT: 4500

##CORS Configuration
# If hosting client and server separately, you may need to configure CORS
# in packages/game-server/src/core/server.ts